  "notes": "D13 EDG is modeled as a System node participating in the consequence (concurrent inoperability driving the TS 3.8.1.1.b 72-hour violation) rather than as a BACKED_UP_BY backup, since it was itself inoperable during the overlap window, not an available backup. The 'remaining Limerick Unit 1 EDGs were operable during this period' statement is generic design-context/safety-consequence language, not a specific stated backup relationship for the failure chain, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was asserted. Previous occurrence LER keys were taken as literally stated in the narrative (2016, 2013, and 2019-002-00); the two undated failures (2016, 2013) lack full LER numbers so key format approximates 'unit-year'."
